WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.560
(Upbeat Music)

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:07.680
(Music Cuts Out)

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.680
One of Us (In Flashback)

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:21.500
(Upbeat Music Continues)

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.460
I think this is in focus.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:23.680
I want to go attack

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.600
Jake from Vsauce who just moved in

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:26.400
across the street,

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.040
but I don't know where Carmichael is

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.660
so I'm gonna go find him.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:32.940
Is Carmichael in here?

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:35.160
Wren: I came looking for you.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:37.120
Vsauce is at their office

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:37.620
right now,

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.120
right?

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.360
They don't have batteries for

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:40.320
their remotes,

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.860
so Jake texted me, he's like

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:43.300
"Hey can you bring us some batteries?"

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:44.580
We'll bring them batteries

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.920
over their dead bodies!

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:13.440
(Laughing, yelling, and nerf gun noises)

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:15.760
Jake: (Chuckles) Hello. Oh! You have a GoPro on it!

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:16.920
Welcome to the neighborhood!

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:17.880
Thank you!

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:20.920
Ah! Come here! Good to see you guys!

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.080
Oh! Good to see -- Let me hug you

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:24.600
Good to see you!

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.060
This is the only reason I moved next to you guys

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:26.560
so I could take batteries.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:27.640
Well thank you!

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:29.340
Welcome to the giant empty space that is

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:30.100
the Vsauce office.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:32.720
Cameraman: Have you showed anyone this yet?

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.000
No, this is the first.

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:35.160
I haven't even shown

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:36.400
the Vsauce viewers yet.

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:37.880
You've not even announced that you've

00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:38.920
moved into an office at all.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:39.560
No, not yet.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:40.860
So thanks, Corridor Digital

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.220
for ruining that for me.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.020
There's a lot we gotta do

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:45.860
basically this side of the office is gonna be a studio

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.300
Oh! I think it's the Time Warner Cable man.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:49.140
Hello?

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:50.220
That's disgusting.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.400
Yeah that dude's nasty.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:34.140
He must

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:35.020
never know.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.180
Niko: No you're doing perfect,

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:41.760
don't change that.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.840
(Music fading in)

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.600
(Music)

00:02:58.940 --> 00:02:59.500
Niko: Yeah!

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:01.760
He's stealing second base

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.020
but there's no - (giberish)

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:03.760
Cut

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:05.820
So you're gonna shoot all my stuff

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:06.560
and then move on to 'D' stuff?

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:07.500
We're probably gonna go back and forth.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.280
Back and forth? Cool.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:08.780
Yeah

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:10.540
We'll get me walking off from there

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:11.620
Let's get a shot through the fence

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.900
It's like it's just a wide angle

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:14.100
where you just see

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.440
me walking off and passing him

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:17.060
and that could be like the bystander angle.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:17.860
Ready?

00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:19.980
One

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:21.760
Are you ready?

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:22.260
Three

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:22.760
Two

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.260
One

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:23.960
Action!

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:25.840
Keeping him in total shade like that

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:27.500
makes it so intense.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:29.440
(Wren Laughing)

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:31.020
(Exhales)

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.400
That was not pleasant.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:33.480
(Dog whimper)

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:34.440
(Dog bark)

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:35.300
Obie help!

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.040
Don't just stand there.

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:43.920
Whoa!

00:03:44.180 --> 00:03:44.900
An infared-

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.900
Spencer: So we can see right now

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:47.400
Jake: Oooh!

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:47.960
Spencer: The ceiling

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:48.580
Jake: is hot!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:49.080
Spencer: is 110 degrees

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.720
Jake: That is a hot ceiling.

00:03:51.020 --> 00:03:52.060
This is the coolest thing

00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:53.480
that I didn't know about,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:54.600
but now I do.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:55.160
Okay

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:55.820
here's - here's an interesting fact

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.080
so right here behind this wall

00:03:58.340 --> 00:03:58.840
Jake: Mmhmm

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:00.620
You can see that there's a pillar

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:01.760
Jake: Yeah

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:02.720
Spencer: behind that wall

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.120
Wren: Oh that's cool!

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:05.280
You can even see like the studs in the wall.

00:04:05.900 --> 00:04:07.460
Jake: We're almost at X-Ray Vision.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:08.760
Spencer: That's a misconception.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.380
Thermal does not give you X-Ray vision.

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:11.520
Jake: But I can see studs!

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.320
Spencer: Yes, but that's because there's a temperature difference.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:13.960
Jake: But it's because I can see through--

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.540
But, I mean, if we're being,

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:16.380
you know,

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:17.480
really pedantic about it,

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:18.560
I feel like that's kind of

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:20.300
a little bit of X-Ray.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:21.000
I'm seeing through the wall.

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.720
So I added a bunch of nerf guns

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:23.640
to my Amazon wish list.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:24.140
Wren: Oh my god

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:25.860
So it's gonna be my like "office supply wishlist"

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:26.900
(Wren and Spencer Laughing)

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:27.580
Jake: A whole bunch of--

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.140
Spencer: I mean, they are tax writables

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:29.780
Jake: I think so

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:30.660
Spencer: Yeah!

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:31.160
It's like, we need them.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:33.360
But I love the reviews that people have on Amazon about them

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.940
they're like "Oh this one fires at like

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:36.960
this r-- like rate per minute" it's like all this stuff.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:38.020
Carmichael: And then you can mod them

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:38.620
Jake: Yeah!

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:39.300
Carmichael: Hey Wren!

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:40.980
Jake: Wren?

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.980
Can you Assassin's Creed yourself up the building?

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:45.820
You want me to climb it?

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:46.320
Jake: The pipe.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.840
Carmichael: Yeah, in fact, we challenge you.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:51.520
Jake: I bet you 10 dollars worth of Taco Bell gift cards

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:53.040
that you can't make it up there.

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:54.600
Wren: Dude, that's such a deal!

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:56.540
Jake: That is a deal! That's like a month's worth of food!

00:04:57.340 --> 00:04:59.220
(Laughter)

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.280
Carmichael: Keep going!

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:02.820
Carmichael: The challenge

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:03.720
Jake: Yeah, he can do it.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:05.980
Jake: Look! He's got those little things to hold.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.400
Jake: Those people that are in there are like "What is happening?"

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:09.900
Jake: Well,

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:11.060
Wren: I can't get up that final 10 percent.

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:11.780
Jake: I'm disappointed.

00:05:12.480 --> 00:05:14.400
But you guys-- it was good seeing you guys

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:15.680
But I'll see you guys on Monday

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:17.800
Maybe we can get tacos from the taco truck together.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:19.420
Wren: So, just come by anytime.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:20.340
Jake: Is Freddie here?

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.120
(Laughter)

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:22.840
(Music)

